Voice"},{"text":". The matrix conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" algorithms run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on it unchanged. It is not a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", even when built from one, because a cell edit can give a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"column any number of bits.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A column is any set of vertices. Empty columns and repeated columns are kept. A graph’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop becomes the one bit at its vertex, the hyperedge {v}. ","type":"text"},{"code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the directed form, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the sparse representation of the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hypergraphs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Storage","text":"Storage","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both orientations are stored: n rows of ⌈m\/64⌉ words and m columns of ⌈n\/64⌉ words, with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row and column popcounts cached. "},{"code":"members(ofHyperedgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"incidentHyperedges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each one "},{"code":"BitSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" copy of ⌈n\/64⌉ or ⌈m\/64⌉ words, a cell edit writes two bits in O(1), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"transposed()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the dual, swaps the two orientations in O(1). The storage is 2·n·m\/8 bytes, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the matrix suits dense or small incidence, such as spectral work or hypergraphs with large"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyperedges. Use "},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for sparse incidence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Equality compares cell for cell, with equal shape, so column order counts."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":"’s equality ignores positions."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The unoriented incidence matrix of a hypergraph, an n × m matrix of bits with cell (v, p) set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when vertex ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"text":" is a member of column ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/Encodable-Implementations":{"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix\/encodable-implementations","title":"Encodable Implementations","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/Encodable-Implementations","type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceMatrix"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceMatrix"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The unoriented incidence matrix of a hypergraph, an n × m matrix of bits with cell (v, p) set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a membe